    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Thanks.\r\n\r\nI had been involved with #8703. And what'd happened is we'd backported a whole bunch of the Python 3.11 work to 0.56.4, and it worked well enough that at least other packages test suites could pass.\r\n\r\nFor what I reported now, I'd dumped the python3.11 compatibility patches and then upgraded to 0.57.1.\r\nI had been hoping that 0.57.1 would fix the arm64 crashes we were having with our hacked 0.56.4, but the crashes seem similar.\r\n\r\nIs there an environment variable one can set to get debug symbols for the compiled code? or do you have to modify the njit decorator with debug=True?",
