    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "I couldn't replicate the first test case you had in 9001 because we don't have numba available. I did try running your second test case under gdb.\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ gdb /usr/bin/python3\r\n\r\n(gdb) set args -m unittest -vb numba.tests.test_stencils.TestManyStencils.test_basic40 \r\n(gdb) run\r\nStarting program: /usr/bin/python3 -m unittest -vb numba.tests.test_stencils.TestManyStencils.test_basic40 \r\nDownloading separate debug info for system-supplied DSO at 0xfffff7ffb000                   \r\n[Thread debugging using libthread_db enabled]                                               \r\nUsing host libthread_db library \"/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libthread_db.so.1\".\r\n[New Thread 0xfffff5c5f1a0 (LWP 2622410)]                                                   \r\n[New Thread 0xfffff344f1a0 (LWP 2622411)]\r\n[New Thread 0xfffff0c3f1a0 (LWP 2622412)]\r\ntest_basic40 (numba.tests.test_stencils.TestManyStencils.test_basic40)                      \r\n2 args! ... Downloading separate debug info for /usr/lib/python3.11/lib-dynload/_multiprocessing.cpython-311-aarch64-linux-gnu.so\r\n[New Thread 0xffffdf8761a0 (LWP 2622424)]                                                   \r\n[New Thread 0xffffdf0661a0 (LWP 2622425)]\r\n[New Thread 0xffffde8561a0 (LWP 2622426)]\r\n\r\nThread 7 \"python3\" received signal SIGBUS, Bus error.\r\n[Switching to Thread 0xffffde8561a0 (LWP 2622426)]\r\n0x00000be0d10083ff in ?? ()\r\n(gdb) bt full\r\n#0  0x00000be0d10083ff in ?? ()\r\nNo symbol table info available.\r\n#1  0x0000ffffe062515c in _ZL12parallel_forPvPPcPmS2_S_mmi._omp_fn.0(void) ()\r\n    at numba/np/ufunc/omppool.cpp:205\r\n        r = 3\r\n        j = <optimized out>\r\n        j = <optimized out>\r\n        r = <optimized out>\r\n        count_space = 0xffffde855840\r\n        array_arg_space = 0xffffde855820\r\n        args = 0xffffffffcd90\r\n        dimensions = 0x0\r\n        steps = 0xffffffffca90\r\n        data = <optimized out>\r\n        array_count = 4\r\n        func = 0xf9000be0d10083ff\r\n        arg_len = <optimized out>\r\n        size = 0\r\n        agreed_nthreads = <optimized out>\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf it'd help I could add more of the stack trace, but I think it'd be more useful if I could get some symbols for frame 0.\r\n\r\nMy current debug environment variables are\r\n\r\n```\r\nexport NUMBA_DEBUGINFO=1\r\nexport NUMBA_OPT=0\r\nexport DEBUGINFOD_URLS=https://debuginfod.debian.net\r\n\r\n```",
