  {
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "@detrout - many thanks - the root cause is known - there's nothing to stop LLVM's RuntimeDyld component allocating memory for different objects that reference each other more than 4GB away from each other, which is not permitted even in the large code model for AArch64, so relocations get overflowed leading to incorrect / illegal memory accesses. I want to solve this problem as it seems to be more and more prevalent on all AArch64 systems, but didn't yet get chance to dig into it.",
