  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Ok I had time and rebuilt the numba 0.59.0 and ran it on arm64 and had various segfaults.\r\n\r\nIt felt like things were flakier with TBB enabled so I tried rebuilding without TBB and here's the first segfault runtests hits. \r\n\r\n```\r\ntest_007_collision_checks (numba.tests.test_dictobject.TestDictObject.test_007_collision_checks) ... /home/diane/numba-0.59.0+dfsg/.pybuild/cpython3_3.11/build/numba/tests/test_dictobject.py:738: NumbaTypeSafetyWarning: unsafe cast from uint64 to int64. Precision may be lost.\r\n  d[c1] = v1\r\n\r\nProgram received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.\r\n```\r\n\r\nand some of the output of bt\r\n\r\n```\r\n#0  0x0028000852800028 in ?? ()\r\nNo symbol table info available.\r\n#1  0x0000fffff6193c10 in NRT_MemInfo_call_dtor (mi=0x3003f30) at numba/core/runtime/nrt.cpp:401\r\nNo locals.\r\n#2  0x0000fffff7fbb0dc in NRT_decref ()\r\nNo symbol table info available.\r\n#3  0x0000fffff7217654 in numba::tests::test_dictobject::TestDictObject::test_007_collision_checks::_3clocals_3e::foo[abi:v56][abi:c8tJTC_2fWwGaMLShh6CjAIxrKR0t9qKIYaQ0qDQwmMEsTAA_3d_3d](double, double) (v1=0, v2=0) at test_dictobject.py:740\r\n        d = {meminfo = 0x3003f30 \"\", data = 0x308b0f0 \"\\002\"}\r\n        c1 = 0\r\n        c2 = 0\r\n        bool208 = 0x0\r\n#4  0x0000fffff72177d8 in cpython::numba::tests::test_dictobject::TestDictObject::test_007_collision_checks::_3clocals_3e::foo[abi:v56][abi:c8tJTC_2fWwGaMLShh6CjAIxrKR0t9qKIYaQ0qDQwmMEsTAA_3d_3d](double, double) ()\r\nNo symbol table info available.\r\n#5  0x0000ffffeb483be4 in compile_and_invoke (self=self@entry=0xffffe6afe2b0, args=args@entry=0xffffe68d8140, \r\n    kws=kws@entry=0x0, locals=locals@entry=0x0) at numba/_dispatcher.cpp:769\r\n        cfa = 0xffffe68d8cc0\r\n        cfunc = 0xffffe6826930\r\n        retval = <optimized out>\r\n#6  0x0000ffffeb484680 in Dispatcher_call (self=0xffffe6afe2b0, args=<optimized out>, kws=<optimized out>)\r\n    at numba/_dispatcher.cpp:1052\r\n        tmptype = <optimized out>\r\n--Type <RET> for more, q to quit, c to continue without paging--c\r\n        retval = 0x0\r\n        tys = 0xffffffffd768\r\n        argct = <optimized out>\r\n        i = <optimized out>\r\n        prealloc = {26, 26, -424688800, 65535, 13, 0, 10942576, 0, -424680784, 65535, -10304, 65535, 5112868, 0, -10304, \r\n          65535, 5112868, 0, 10942576, 0, -420503760, 65535, -10224, 65535}\r\n        matches = <optimized out>\r\n        cfunc = <optimized out>\r\n        ts = <optimized out>\r\n        locals = 0x0\r\n        exact_match_required = 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nI've trying with python 3.11.7, llvmlite 0.42.0, and numpy 1.26.4\r\n\r\n\r\nsome maybe useful hardware info.\r\n```\r\ncat /proc/cpuinfo\r\n\r\nprocessor\t: 0\r\nBogoMIPS\t: 50.00\r\nFeatures\t: fp asimd evtstrm aes pmull sha1 sha2 crc32 atomics fphp asimdhp cpuid asimdrdm lrcpc dcpop asimddp ssbs\r\nCPU implementer\t: 0x41\r\nCPU architecture: 8\r\nCPU variant\t: 0x3\r\nCPU part\t: 0xd0c\r\nCPU revision\t: 1\r\n\r\n$ dpkg-architecture \r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH=arm64\r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH_ABI=base\r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH_BITS=64\r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH_CPU=arm64\r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH_ENDIAN=little\r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH_LIBC=gnu\r\nDEB_BUILD_ARCH_OS=linux\r\nDEB_BUILD_GNU_CPU=aarch64\r\nDEB_BUILD_GNU_SYSTEM=linux-gnu\r\nDEB_BUILD_GNU_TYPE=aarch64-linux-gnu\r\nDEB_BUILD_MULTIARCH=aarch64-linux-gnu\r\n\r\n```\r\n",
